__pycache__/
*.pyc
logs/
qwen3-4b-instruct/
qwen3-4b-instruct_uncapped_partial_*/
qwen3-4b-instruct_thinking_contaminated_*/
qwen3-4b-*/
# All Qwen3 model_tag extraction subtrees are reproducible tensor/rows artifacts.
# Result JSONs are tracked by COPYING to the probe root (amendment_*_result.json),
# never from under a model_tag dir. Covers Amendment X sizes (qwen3-1.7b-bnb-4bit/,
# qwen3-8b-bnb-4bit/, qwen3-14b-bnb-4bit/) and any future Qwen3 tag.
qwen3-*/

# Hidden-state extraction outputs (exploratory tier). These land under
# <model_tag>/hidden_states/ and are large reproducible tensor artifacts
# (per-arm safetensors + manifest + rows). The current model_tag dir
# (qwen3-4b-instruct/) is already fully ignored above; this anchored rule is a
# defensive guard so a FUTURE model_tag's hidden_states tree is never staged by
# `git add -A`, regardless of which model_tag dir is or isn't blanket-ignored.
*/hidden_states*/

# SAE smoke outputs are reproducible exploratory artifacts. They may include
# tensor slices from hidden activations, so keep them local unless a governed
# artifact-publication decision explicitly whitelists a subset.
*/sae_smokes/
*/sae_runs/
*/sae_feature_analysis/
*/sae_feature_directions/

# Amendment Z cross-family extraction subtrees (z_<tag>/, z_smoke_<tag>/) and the
# queue logs (z_logs/) are large reproducible tensor/rows artifacts. The scored
# result JSONs are tracked at the probe root as amendment_z_*_result.json (which
# does NOT match z_*/), never from under an extraction dir.
z_*/

# Amendment SR sampled-decode seed-robustness extraction subtrees
# (sr_<tag>_seed<N>/, sr_smoke_<tag>/) + queue logs (sr_logs/) are large
# reproducible tensor/rows artifacts. Scored result JSONs are tracked at the
# probe root as amendment_sr_*_result.json (does NOT match sr_*/).
sr_*/
